{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghoUBAnfKE84t8US7xQm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fit gives Dq ≈ 1037 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 822 cm⁻¹, so Δ = 10Dq ≈ 10 370 cm⁻¹ and 10Dq/B ≈ 12.6. The complex is high-spin d7 (⁴T₁g ground term), and the fit was run on the full octahedral d7 Tanabe–Sugano matrices.\n\n**Assignment**\n- 9 180 cm⁻¹ is ⁴T₁g(F) → ⁴T₂g (ν₁).\n- 19 550 cm⁻¹ is ⁴T₁g(F) → ⁴A₂g (ν₂).\n- 20 320 cm⁻¹ is ⁴T₁g(F) → ⁴T₁g(P) (ν₃).\n\n**Fit quality**\n- The predicted bands are 9 180.5, 19 549.7 and 20 320.0 cm⁻¹. The residuals are about 0.5, −0.3 and 0 cm⁻¹.\n- A second, independent ratio fit gave Dq ≈ 1045 and B ≈ 814 cm⁻¹, which is consistent.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The three spin-allowed bands do not fix the Racah parameter C. The fit assumed C ≈ 4 499 cm⁻¹, and the spin-allowed manifold is insensitive to it. C is therefore an assumption, not a result, and I report it as null in the JSON line.\n- ν₂ and ν₃ sit very close together, which means the ⁴T₁g(F) and ⁴T₁g(P) levels are strongly mixed. That is unusual, because ν₂ and ν₃ are normally further apart in Co²⁺ complexes. It may reflect an experimental assignment issue, for example a doublet-state feature borrowing intensity, but the fit accounts for all three bands.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1037, \"B\": 822, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"High-spin d7 fit of the three spin-allowed bands (ν1, ν2, ν3) reproduces them to within about 0.5 cm^-1, and C is not constrained by these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6577,"cache_read_input_tokens":7985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6577,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a